-- R10 — Carver trend/carry forecast line on cards; FX option pricer (QuantLib-checked) for option cards and expressions.
-- Owner request, 25 Oct 2026 (project thread "Find open-source code for macro workflows"): from a shortlist of openly
-- licensed quant code, the owner said "do both" to (1) Carver's EWMAC trend and carry forecasts in the trend monitor
-- and (2) a QuantLib-checked FX option pricer for the digests. Code: supabase/functions/_shared/forecast.ts (appended to
-- the dash-trend report) and scripts/fxopt/ (fxopt.py, test_fxopt.py); note docs/carver_and_fxopt.md.
-- To be proposed with this exact statement once the dash-trend deploy and the Drive copy of fxopt.py are done
-- (dash.propose_rule; apply_after = the next Sunday 20:00 SGT window unless the owner replies "oppose R10").
-- To put it in force before the Sunday window (one line in the Supabase SQL editor, project diiwqbxyhtgvozhncoef):
--   update dash.rules set status = 'in_force', decided_at = now(), apply_after = now() where rid = 'R10' and status = 'proposed';
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "Carver trend/carry forecast line on cards; FX option pricer (QuantLib-checked) for option cards and expressions", "body": "CARVER FORECASTS AND THE FX OPTION PRICER (owner, 25 Oct 2026). Two read-only tools for evidence and pricing; neither is a gate and neither changes the trade test.\n\n1. CARVER LINE. At the evidence step run execute_sql (same project) `select run_date, substring(report from 'CARVER FORECASTS.*END_FORECASTS') as fc from dash.trend_run order by run_date desc limit 1;` (the trend monitor's latest run, 08:30 SGT on the previous weekday, so data to the New York close before last; the forecasts move slowly and the lag is stated, not corrected). The block has one human line per asset and machine lines FORECAST|run_date|asset|last_date|f8|f16|f32|f64|trend|carry|combined on a -20..+20 scale (|10| = average conviction, + = long the asset; for UST2Y/5Y/10Y/30Y, EUR10Y_AAA and JGB10Y + = long bonds, i.e. lower yields). For every NEW card, every TESTED line and every open card at review whose proxy is, or tracks, a monitor asset (FX pairs by name; ES/^GSPC = SPX, NQ/^NDX = NDX, CL = WTI, BZ = BRENT, NG = NATGAS, GC = GOLD, SI = SILVER, HG = COPPER, ZT/ZF/ZN/ZB or ^TNX = UST2Y/UST5Y/UST10Y/UST30Y, Bund = EUR10Y_AAA, JGB = JGB10Y, NKD/^N225 = NKY, ^HSI = HSI, ^HSCE = HSCEI, ^KS11 = KOSPI, ^TWII = TWSE, ^AXJO = AS51, ^NSEI = NIFTY, ^STOXX50E = SX5E, CSI300), print one line in the card's evidence: \"CARVER: trend <+x> · carry <+y or n/a> · combined <+z> (as of <last_date>)\", signed for the card's direction (multiply by -1 for a short). When the signed combined is -10 or below, the card's case against names it (\"trend and carry against: -12\"); nothing is lowered or vetoed automatically. If the query returns no block, print \"CARVER: n/a (no forecast block)\". Carry is a policy-rate proxy (BIS): for INR, IDR, KRW, CNH it differs from NDF-implied carry, which R07's forward points measure directly and which wins for the card's own arithmetic.\n\n2. PRICER. The FX option pricer fxopt.py (Python standard library; every formula checked against QuantLib 1.44) is the Drive file titled \"fxopt.py\" in folder 1LLeuELL8CLpWmtcywt2DiCpJVopNgyqm: read it with read_file_content once per run, save it to disk unchanged and run `python3 -I fxopt.py '<json>'` (a JSON list prices several legs; the usage text is at the top of the file). Use it for every R01 convexity card (NEW and at review), for any option expression a card names (R09's crowd=with cards, WASHOUT WATCH), and for option ideas from the feeds that reach THE TRADE TEST. Inputs: spot = REF; fwd = REF + R07's points for the expiry tenor (else rd and rf in percent, labelled est.); vol in percent = an implied vol found on the web today with its source and time, else the trend monitor's rv20 for the pair (`select rv20 from dash.trend_state where asset_id = '<PAIR>' order by run_date desc limit 1`) labelled \"realised rv20, not implied\"; atm, rr25, bf25 when a smile is found (then the model is vanna-volga). Print one line: \"PRICER: <structure> <price as % of payout or of base notional> (<model>, vol <x>% <source>) · delta <d> · p_touch or p_exercise <p>\". For R01 cards the R01 MARK SCRIPT premium remains the card's p0; the PRICER line is a cross-check, and a gap above 2 points of payout between them is explained in one clause (usually carry or vol source). Knock-out and knock-in barriers may be priced and named as cheaper expressions but are not carded (R01 has no barrier struct). A model probability is never written as a market-implied odd: the yellow-tag rule (\"n/a (desk)\") is unchanged. If the file cannot be read or the script fails, print \"PRICER: n/a (<reason>)\" and carry on.", "rationale": "Owner, 25 Oct 2026 (thread 'Find open-source code for macro workflows'): use openly licensed quant code in the book. Carver's EWMAC trend and carry forecasts (Systematic Trading, pysystemtrade) give each card a graded, systematic read of trend and carry on one scale; the FX option pricer adds barriers, delta-strike conventions and a vanna-volga smile to the R01 digital/touch maths, with every formula cross-checked against QuantLib.", "evidence": "fxopt.py vs QuantLib 1.44 on 5 pairs: vanillas, digitals (terms and base pay), one-touch (expiry and hit), single barriers, delta conventions, strike from delta: worst difference below 3e-11 of spot; vanna-volga barriers 3.3e-7 of spot (finite-difference bumps). The dashboard's existing R01 digital / one-touch / spread formulas match QuantLib to 4e-15. Carver forecasts run through the trend monitor's own code on live Yahoo and BIS data on 25 Oct 2026; FDM 1.13; average |forecast| 7.8 per speed with Carver's published scalars (so a 10 here is a stronger-than-average signal).", "revert_if": "Revert if a weekly review finds the CARVER line mis-signed for the card's direction on 2 or more cards, the forecast block missing on 3 or more runs in a week, or PRICER lines failing or more than 2 points of payout from the R01 MARK SCRIPT premium without an explanation on 3 or more cards.", "supersedes": null, "review_due": "2026-12-06", "source": "owner"}$j$::jsonb);
